\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Schematic diagram of the spin-dependent neutron intensity in the polarized neutron scattering experiment. The incident beam with intensity $N_0$ is polarized by the \ce {Cu2MnAl} polarizer and then scattered by the sample with the spin-dependent cross sections $\Sigma ^{++}$, $\Sigma ^{+-}$, $\Sigma ^{-+}$, and $\Sigma ^{--}$. The scattered neutrons are analyzed by the $^3$He-NSF~ with transmission $T_a$ and polarization efficiency $p_a$. The measured intensity $I^{++}$ is given by the sum of the contributions from the four spin-scattering channels when \ce {Cu2MnAl} and $^3$He-NSF~ are both polarized in the same direction.}}{7}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:appendix}{{8}{7}{Schematic diagram of the spin-dependent neutron intensity in the polarized neutron scattering experiment. The incident beam with intensity $N_0$ is polarized by the \ce {Cu2MnAl} polarizer and then scattered by the sample with the spin-dependent cross sections $\Sigma ^{++}$, $\Sigma ^{+-}$, $\Sigma ^{-+}$, and $\Sigma ^{--}$. The scattered neutrons are analyzed by the \Hensf ~ with transmission $T_a$ and polarization efficiency $p_a$. The measured intensity $I^{++}$ is given by the sum of the contributions from the four spin-scattering channels when \ce {Cu2MnAl} and \Hensf ~ are both polarized in the same direction}{figure.8}{}}
\newlabel{eq:Ipp_Ipm}{{A2}{7}{}{equation.A.2}{}}
